# (gh release download v12.1.0 --repo kennypassenier/kp-themes -p SHA256SUMS), for
# every file vendored under static/kp/ with the package's own paths kept, so the
# relative url('../fonts/…') references and the JS import closure stay valid.
# Checked by a unit test, so the gate holds offline: these hashes say "our copies
# are unmodified AND are the tag we claim". Bumping kp-themes means re-copying the
# files AND refreshing this file. The seventeen js/ modules are the closure kp-themes'
# own gates/check-closure.mjs protects for this consumer since 7.0.0 (fix-56):
# the six theme modules, js/effects.js, js/as-of.js and the nine js/effects/ hooks;
# The other js/ modules (the whole framework-free component set: wizard,
# datatable, palette, …) are embedded only with the `webapp` feature, for a
# project's own browser app (feat-webapp-1).
# dist/kp-themes.css is the release's own bundle of themes, components, layout,
# utilities and every register (D2, 2026-09-09) — see docs/DASHBOARD.md.
